---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro'
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro'

// Change this date whenever the terms' substance changes (not on every build).
const LAST_UPDATED = 'October 9, 2026'
---
<Base title="Terms of Service" description="The terms for using Ravenburst, in plain language: your writing is yours.">
  <Nav />
  <main id="main" class="pt-32 pb-20 px-6 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-serif font-bold mb-3">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-rb-muted text-sm mb-10">Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-rb-muted leading-relaxed">
      <section class="bg-rb-surface border border-rb-border rounded-xl p-6">
        <p class="text-rb-text"><strong>In plain language:</strong> buy the app, use it honestly, don’t redistribute it — and your writing is always yours.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-semibold text-rb-text mb-3">Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          Ravenburst is made and sold by Pitts Family Productions LLC (“we”, “us”). These terms are an agreement
          between you and us.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-semibold text-rb-text mb-3">Your license</h2>
        <p>
          Buying Ravenburst gives you a personal, non-transferable license to install and use it on up to 3 computers.
          You may not redistribute, resell or reverse-engineer it, or share your activation code.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-semibold text-rb-text mb-3">Your writing</h2>
        <p>
          Everything you write in Ravenburst belongs entirely to you. We claim no rights to your content, and it is
          stored on your own computer and wherever you choose to back it up.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-semibold text-rb-text mb-3">Trial</h2>
        <p>
          The free trial lasts 7 days. When it ends you can still open, write in and save your projects; exporting
          is paused until you activate a license.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-semibold text-rb-text mb-3">Refunds</h2>
        <p>
          You can have a full refund within 30 days of purchase, no questions asked — email
          <a href="mailto:support@ravenburst.com" class="text-rb-accent hover:underline">support@ravenburst.com</a>.
          Once refunded, the license is deactivated. Kickstarter pledges follow Kickstarter’s own rules.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-semibold text-rb-text mb-3">Updates</h2>
        <p>
          Ravenburst checks for updates and, where your system allows, downloads them in the background. An update
          installs only when you quit or choose to restart; you can turn automatic checks off in Preferences. Your
          license covers updates within the major version it names.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-semibold text-rb-text mb-3">Test features</h2>
        <p>
          Features marked as test features, such as Google Drive backup, are offered early and may change or be
          removed. Don’t rely on them as your only backup.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-semibold text-rb-text mb-3">No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          Ravenburst is provided “as is”. We work hard to make it reliable, but we can’t be liable for lost work or
          other damages. Keep backups of your projects — the app’s snapshots and Git Backup are there to help.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-semibold text-rb-text mb-3">Limits on liability</h2>
        <p>
          As far as the law allows, we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses, and our total liability
          for any claim about Ravenburst is limited to the amount you paid for it. Nothing in these terms takes away
          rights you have under consumer protection laws that can’t be waived.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-semibold text-rb-text mb-3">Contact</h2>
        <p><a href="mailto:support@ravenburst.com" class="text-rb-accent hover:underline">support@ravenburst.com</a></p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
